WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:05.940
Manatsu needs to remain in the hospital for a few more days.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.440
But I'm feeling fine...

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.400
You hit your head pretty hard, kid.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.780
And we still have more tests to run.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.200
You should let them make sure you're okay.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.530
Pitz says so, too.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.790
Animals actually aren't allowed in the medical center, you know...

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.790
Akari taught me a magic spell to help you feel better, Daichi!

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.790
No way...

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.760
Don't, don't, don't—

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.760
Belly Button Forte!

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.090
D-Don't do that! Hide it!

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.840
Restraint! Restraint!

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.180
You don't feel better?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.770
No... When you're wearing a dress,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.770
Belly Button Forte is more of an offensive spell than a healing one.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.190
Yes, this is Shibuya.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.780
Yes, he's here.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.450
Yes. That will be fine.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.830
Yes, understood.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:03.120
Teppei, Commander Nishikubo wants to see you.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.290
Right.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.920
I hope we can all live together again!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.880
And make dinner and stuff!

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.300
Y-You're right.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.930
It may have only been a little while ago,

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.430
but it feels like an image from my distant past.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.470
Right now, it feels so far away from me.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:28.770
Hana...

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.150
Did I do something bad to you?

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.620
Thanks to you, I found out who I really am,

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.330
and answered a question
I've had for a very long time.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:51.250
Did you know that the Machine Goodfellows are powered by Orgone energy?

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.670
Pitz told me.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.880
Didn't you suspect that I might be your enemy?

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.800
Not for a second.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:02.390
I knew you would save Daichi.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.600
Next time I return to the Kill-T-Gang,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.640
I might not be the same person.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:12.480
Teppei?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.360
Don't have so much faith in me.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.070
Teppei!

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:34.800
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.460
Always go

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.880
On my own

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.100
Always go

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:53.730
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:02:53.940 --> 00:03:01.110
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:07.200
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:16.130
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.670
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:29.310
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:35.360
All we have left is the future

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:41.780
Please become our reason to continue living

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:48.490
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.630
Things are moving quickly now.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.920
Registration code 10878F.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:04.220
This is one of the members selected for participation in the Kivotos Plan.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.010
He's currently held in a cryogenic sleep aboard
the <i>Tenkaido</i>'s Ark block.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.980
They are attempting to capture him.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.480
We want you to protect him.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.060
I've decided you are appropriate for this mission

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.690
due to your combat training.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.480
Who is he?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.940
He is a prisoner undergoing sentencing

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.110
for assault and attempted murder.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.370
A prisoner is a Kivotos Plan member?

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:28.950
Well...

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.750
It would seem that he was selected based on genetic qualifications.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.880
His name is Arashi Eiji.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.830
"Arashi"?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.590
He's the one who gave you,

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.300
a Designer's Child, your genes.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.970
It might be appropriate to say he's your father.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.020
This mission is a collaborative effort with the <i>Tenkaido</i>, isn't it?

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.310
If that's the case, it shouldn't be necessary for me to go to space.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:01.320
I've decided not to appraise headquarters of the existence of your Kill-T-Gang.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.280
You understand what I'm saying, right?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.410
You're saying that we're operating independently, aren't you?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.910
Starry Sky's Picture Book

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.250
This is <i>Red Papillon</i>.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.840
I estimate fifteen minutes until contact with the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.420
This is Tanegashima. Roger that.

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:35.770
Are you sure sending Akari with him was the right decision?

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.350
This is a pretty dangerous mission.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.980
It would be impossible to get approval from command for something like this.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.360
Doubly so when we have a commander

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.820
who identifies with the Intercept Faction, and actively opposes the Ark Faction.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.450
If they're willing to use things like violence to achieve their goals,

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.240
we need to take the initiative and seize him before they can.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.210
And in order to do that, we needed a reason to send Teppei to the <i>Tenkaido</i>...

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.130
So the pretext for this operation is Akari wanting to see her mother?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.050
It makes perfect sense.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.090
I'm amazed she didn't get mad,
being used for a mission like that.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.970
She thought it was hilarious.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.810
It might be possible that Akari really did want to see her mother...

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.530
Well, she is her daughter, after all.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:31.030
But aren't they going after Arashi Eiji because they've begun to suspect

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.490
the relationship between Teppei and the Kill-T-Gang after the recent attack?

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:38.250
Teppei is quarantined in this base, so they can't touch him.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:42.630
That's why they're going after Eiji, isn't it?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:46.210
And we're just going to send Teppei right into the middle of it.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.720
That, however, isn't logical at all.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.510
But...

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.300
You have a plan, don't you?

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.390
Well, at this point, we're all in this together.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.350
My apologies.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.190
<i>Red Papillon</i> is about to rendezvous with the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.300
Is something wrong?

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.510
No... It's nothing.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.400
I'm so glad you came!

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.980
How rich do you have to be to fly into space just to see your mom?

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.860
Well, Governor Yomatsuri hasn't been down to the surface in years...

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.320
They probably made an exception in this case.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.700
You've really grown up.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.280
Well, yeah I guess.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:00.660
I was so happy when I heard that you wanted to see me.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.090
Parents...

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.170
This whole thing is kind of foreign to me.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:13.050
The pilot's pretty cute...

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:13.800
Hey, now...

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.510
I hope we'll have time to catch up later.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:22.060
Hey, there was another shuttle docked when we arrived.

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.480
Where'd it depart from?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.060
That was our regular supply shuttle.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.070
Regular?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.950
There are twenty-five containers in total.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.320
All of them have been brought aboard.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.370
Container loading has been confirmed.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.660
Thanks for the help.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.370
Yo.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.210
Time to get to work, huh?

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:49.550
I'll help you.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.800
You're not going to spend some time with your mother?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.090
This seems much more interesting.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.340
And...

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.390
If you're going to use this, you need me!

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:10.520
The corridor to the Kivotos Plan's cryogenic hibernation block—the Ark block—

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.070
is insulated by dozens of bulkheads.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.110
The outside world has been told that

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.910
it's merely a long-distance spaceflight staffed by qualified volunteers.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:22.290
But in reality, it's a secret plan for carefully chosen elites to escape Earth.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.000
There would be people rioting in the streets if this got out.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:31.920
Evidently my mother has requested that I be included in the third group of sleepers.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:35.760
The Ark Faction thinks anyone who stays on Earth will be destroyed.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.130
They're far too pessimistic.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.050
I'm definitely with the Intercept Faction.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:41.760
Huh?

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.270
What's wrong?

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:46.440
Several of the alarms in this sector have been disabled.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.360
We're not the only ones skulking about.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:54.780
I bet they snuck in on the supply shuttle we saw at the dock when we arrived.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:55.990
Oh, please.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:59.160
So long as I'm here, we still have the advantage.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:02.240
Logical, logical... Open sesame!

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.620
We need to be quick.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.750
Hey, how much do you know—

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.460
Just call me Akari, Teppei.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.420
How much do you know about this mission, Akari?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.800
If you're referring to the genes you share with the target,

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.510
they didn't tell me, but I know anyway.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.680
You've learned all this through your hacking?

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.480
Well, yeah, but...

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.940
When I looked at you,

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.480
I just suddenly wanted to meet this person.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:43.830
Numbers 10801F through 10900F.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.040
This is it.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.870
It's finally time.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:54.550
Teppei...

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:58.220
Number 10878F.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:58.840
I'm unloading it.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.600
This man is my gene donor?

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.690
He doesn't look much older than me...

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:17.110
This is bad...

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.240
They've entered the area.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.860
That was faster than I expected.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.410
They'll be here before we can wake him.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.250
Doesn't this sector have emergency blast doors?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.040
Yeah.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.170
Can you close them without triggering the alarm?

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.710
That would be impossible...

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.590
If I were normal, that is.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.340
Leave it to the magical girl!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:45.140
We'll use this time to wake him up and get him through the emergency hatch in the back.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.920
Please remain calm.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.000
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.250
This is not part of the original Kivotos Plan program.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:24.180
You've been woken up early for another reason.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.600
Do you feel all right?

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.940
I'll ask again.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.900
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.660
It's Teppei, isn't it?

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.790
Why do you know my name?

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.510
Because I gave it to you.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.970
I could tell with one look.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.550
Damn, you've grown up.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:13.930
We have to hurry.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.600
They'll get that door unlocked soon.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.690
Am I their target?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.700
You seem to be quite the hacker, miss.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.620
Give me a line in, and I can do anything!

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.290
After all, I'm a magical girl!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.250
That's delightful!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.050
The target's gone.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:48.090
Looks like somebody got here before us.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.470
Come to think of it, there was a Tanegashima shuttle here, too.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.480
I can't believe they beat us.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:08.160
I think that got them off our trail.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.410
I'm impressed you came up with this.

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:12.410
Sorry for bothering you.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:20.960
Okay, let's go.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.000
Wait!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.270
Thanks.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.020
Sure...

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.060
Is she your girlfriend?

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:42.900
No, she isn't.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:48.650
When we were your age, your mom and dad were already in love with each other.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.870
My "dad"...

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.500
By the way...

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.710
What is a "dad"?

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:10.430
I don't have a dad.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.470
An ambush, huh?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.520
There's just one, though.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.890
I'm amazed you could tell.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.020
Do you have any weapons?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.020
This conceals a tranquilizer gun.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.230
Okay.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:26.190
Guess we'll use that... and these.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:35.870
Empty spacesuits?

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.680
Are you okay?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:19.540
Thanks.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:24.120
There's a high probability that they know where we are now.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.840
It's too dangerous to stay here.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.050
Let's look for some spacesuits.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.550
You're going outside?

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.430
The external hatches aren't controlled electronically.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.010
You're going to need a key.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:37.800
Found it.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:39.890
Plastic explosives?

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:43.810
We'll use this to get outside, make for the dock, and then steal their shuttle.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.730
But we have our own shuttle.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.860
Given the nature of their operation,

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.820
their shuttle will be ready to leave at a moment's notice.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.740
Stealing it's going to be faster.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:57.780
With your magic, we can easily take over their navigation systems, right?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:16:59.450
That's insane!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.580
Just do what daddy tells you.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.230
Trouble with bulkhead 1883.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:26.940
What?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.730
What's this?

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:29.650
What's wrong?

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.500
That's their shuttle.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.210
He's obviously armed.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.170
What?

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.180
Hey, Teppei, your dad—

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:58.220
Listen.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:02.260
Would you stop calling yourself that?

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.810
I'm not sure how you look at this situation,

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:09.270
but I don't think of you that way.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.940
And it's not like that.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.950
I'm not who you think I am.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.800
I'm sorry...

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.050
I haven't even been around enough to read you a picture book.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.020
I really do regret it.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:53.190
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:54.400
My tranquilizer gun?

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:57.610
When did you...?!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.320
Teppei!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.200
Why?

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.490
Aren't we stealing the shuttle?

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:05.660
Sorry.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:07.000
I lied.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:11.250
That shot actually wounded me worse than I thought.

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.590
I can't protect you two.

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.510
And these guys are pros.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.380
I can tell because they're a lot like me.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:24.260
But because I'm their target, you two will be safe if I surrender.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:27.720
However, if they're really just after my genes,

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:31.400
wouldn't that also make Teppei their target?

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.690
I don't know why Teppei was sent here.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.860
Maybe someone wanted him to see me?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:43.490
Either way, I'm sure this was
something that the adults wanted.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:49.000
But if he's got a girl like you with him, I don't need to worry.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.330
Take care of my son.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.290
Teppei's dad...

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.420
That does have a nice ring to it.

00:19:57.210 --> 00:19:59.550
Try not to worry about me.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.800
I'm a criminal, after all.

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:13.980
His assault and attempted murder were both to protect Teppei.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:16.900
He tried to prevent Teppei, his child,

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:21.450
from being used as a test subject by Macbeth Enterprises.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:29.490
Was having Teppei meet him your true goal?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:33.120
You really are a romantic.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:53.140
These were Commander Nishikubo's orders?

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:57.560
I lied to you for the sake of the mission.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:20:59.860
I'm really sorry.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.780
Whatever your reason was,

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:06.280
you truly can't even imagine

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:10.200
how happy I was to see you.

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:27.050
When she looks at you,

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:32.520
Governor Yomatsuri seems so kind.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:37.900
Ah... Sorry.

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:39.860
That was a weird thing to say.

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:47.410
He looked at you the same way that my mom looked at me.

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:56.620
We have reason to suspect that the kidnappers were employed by Salty Dog.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:59.630
They've denied any involvement, of course.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:01.800
I'm sorry.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:04.090
The mission was a failure.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:07.930
Ultimately, it all worked out.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:11.850
It seems that Arashi Eiji managed to escape when the shuttle landed.

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:15.020
His whereabouts are currently unknown.

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:17.690
Good work.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.190
Get some rest.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:26.320
I'm sorry...

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:32.030
I haven't even been around enough to read you a picture book.

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:42.000
My dad, huh?

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:55.020
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:55.020 --> 00:23:00.480
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.320
aren't always good things

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:13.030
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:22.460
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:30.680
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:36.720
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:42.600
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:45.610
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:53.820
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:57.240
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.240 --> 00:24:03.380
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:18.060
The Kivotos Plan was proposed as a last hope for humanity's survival.

00:24:18.470 --> 00:24:22.140
But many conspiracies lurk in the background.

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:25.440
And Hirose, from Salty Dog,

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:28.610
tries to kidnap Hana for the Kivotos Plan.

00:24:29.150 --> 00:24:31.780
Next time, on episode 6 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:33.820
Kivotos Plan

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:33.820
Kivotos Plan.

00:24:33.820 --> 00:24:36.410
Earth Engine, expand!
